To use the Virtual Fly Brain Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool, follow these steps: Open Claude Desktop and go to Settings, navigate to the MCP section, add a new MCP server with the settings: Server Name: virtual-fly-brain, Type: HTTP, Server URL: https://vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org. Alternatively, use the Configuration JSON or locate your Claude configuration file and add the VFB3-MCP server to your configuration. For GitHub Copilot setup, open VS Code with GitHub Copilot installed, open Settings, search for "MCP" in the settings search, find the MCP Servers setting, add the server URL, and give it a name like "Virtual Fly Brain". For other MCP-compatible clients that support HTTP servers, use the provided JSON configuration. For Gemini setup, use custom Python/Node.js clients that support MCP, and for application development, use the mcp and google-genai libraries to connect.

```
{
"mcpServers": {
"virtual-fly-brain": {
"type": "http",
"url": "https://vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org",
"tools": ["*"]
}
}
}
```
